\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lift up your hearts! We lift them,
\par Lord, to Thee;
\par Here at Thy feet none other may
\par we see;
\par Lift up your hearts! E'en so, with 
\par one accord,
\par We lift them up, we lift them 
\par to the Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Above the level of the former years
\par The mire of sin, the slough of guilty
\par fears,
\par The mist of doubt, the blight of
\par love's decay,
\par O Lord of Light, lift all our hearts 
\par to- day!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Above the swamps of subterfuge
\par and shame,
\par The deeds, the thoughts that honour
\par may not name,
\par The halting tongue that dares not 
\par tell the whole,
\par O Lord of Truth, lift every Christian
\par soul!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lift every gift that Thou Thyself 
\par hast given;
\par Low lies the best till lifted  up to
\par heaven:
\par Low lie the bounding heart, the
\par teeming brain,
\par Till, sent from God, they mount 
\par to God gain. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then, as the trumpet- call, in 
\par after years:
\par Lift up your hearts, rings pealing 
\par in our ears,
\par Still shall those hearts respond,
\par with full accord:
\par We lift them up, we lift them to 
\par the Lord!
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

